<%# English version of the policy, for English-speaking students. French is the
    reference version — Practice-BR is established in France and the supervisory
    authority is the CNIL. Header and language switch live in home/privacy.html.erb.
    Keep both versions in sync when the policy changes. %>

<div class="rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8" style="background: var(--brand-mist); border: 1px solid var(--brand-tint);">
  <p class="leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink);">
    In short: we keep only what the platform needs to work, we never sell your data
    to anyone, we use no advertising trackers, and we delete your data whenever you
    ask us to. Everything below explains that in detail — no fine print.
  </p>
</div>

<div style="color: var(--ink);">

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Practice-BR is a service published by <strong>Daisy Oliani</strong>, sole trader
    (<em>entrepreneur individuel</em>), 43 Clos des Cascades, 93160 Noisy-le-Grand,
    France — SIRET 85 194 793 700 013.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Daisy Oliani is the data controller for the processing described here, within the
    meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). For anything related to
    your personal data, write to
    <a href="mailto:contato@practicebr.com" class="font-semibold underline" style="color: var(--brand);">contato@practicebr.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul class="mb-4 space-y-2 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
    <li><strong>Sign-up:</strong> your email address, first name (optional), language, Portuguese level and your role (student or teacher).</li>
    <li><strong>Password:</strong> stored only in hashed form — not even we can read it.</li>
    <li><strong>Platform use:</strong> your answers to exercises (including the texts you write), your scores, the dates of your attempts, your teacher's comments and the ratings you give to activities.</li>
    <li><strong>Audio:</strong> if you answer out loud, the recording is used only to produce the transcript and is <strong>deleted immediately afterwards</strong>. Only the transcribed text is kept.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment:</strong> your Stripe subscription identifiers and its status. Your card details go straight to Stripe and <strong>never pass through our servers</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> if you allow them in your browser, we store the technical address needed to send them.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> server access logs, used for security and to investigate errors.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">3. Why we use it (legal bases)</h2>
  <ul class="mb-4 space-y-2 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
    <li><strong>Performance of the contract:</strong> creating your account, showing activities, marking exercises and tracking your progress.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> billing your subscription and keeping accounting records.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> keeping the platform secure and preventing fraud and abuse.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent:</strong> sending notifications and reminders — which you can turn off at any time in your preferences.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    If you are the student of a teacher on the platform, that teacher can see your
    activities, your answers and your scores — that is how they follow and correct
    your work.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">4. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    We do not sell or hand over your data for advertising. We rely on a few
    processors, each receiving only the data needed for its job:
  </p>
  <%= render "home/privacy_subprocessors", service_label: "Processor", purpose_label: "Purpose",
             purposes: {
               "Heroku (Salesforce)" => "Hosting the application and the database",
               "Anthropic (Claude)"  => "Marking written answers and generating activities",
               "OpenAI (Whisper)"    => "Transcribing spoken answers",
               "Stripe"              => "Processing payments",
               "Resend"              => "Sending the platform's emails",
               "Cloudinary"          => "Storing activity images and audio",
               "Sentry (European Union)" => "Logging technical errors, with no personal data"
             } %>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    <strong>Transfers outside the European Union:</strong> these providers run
    servers in the United States, so your data is processed there. We only work with
    providers offering the contractual safeguards required by the GDPR for such
    transfers. <strong>Sentry is the exception:</strong> error data is stored in the
    European Union, in its Frankfurt region.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">5. Artificial intelligence</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Your written and spoken answers are marked automatically by artificial
    intelligence. Two things matter here:
  </p>
  <ul class="mb-4 space-y-2 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
    <li>We send the AI <strong>only the text of your answer</strong> and the marking criteria for the question. Neither your name nor your email address is sent.</li>
    <li>The AI's score is not the final word: your teacher sees the correction, can comment on it and can override what the machine got wrong. If you want a human to review a correction, ask your teacher or write to us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">6. Cookies</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    We only use strictly necessary cookies: the ones that keep you signed in and the
    ones that protect forms against fraud. <strong>No Google Analytics, no social
    media pixel, no advertising cookie</strong> — and the platform's fonts, icons and
    scripts are served from our own domain, so opening a page here tells no other
    company about it. That is why there is no cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    For as long as your account is active, so that you and your teacher can follow
    your progress over time. Once it has gone unused for long enough, the data no
    longer serves any purpose — so we delete it.
  </p>
  <ul class="mb-4 space-y-2 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
    <li><strong>Account with no activity:</strong> deleted <strong>3 years</strong> after your last activity on the platform.</li>
    <li><strong>Free trial not taken further:</strong> deleted <strong>12 months</strong> after the trial ends.</li>
    <li><strong>Active subscription:</strong> the account is kept for as long as the subscription runs — the relationship hasn't ended.</li>
    <li><strong>Accounting records:</strong> kept for <strong>10 years</strong>, as accounting and tax law require. That is a legal obligation, and a deletion request cannot override it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    <strong>You get a warning first.</strong> Deletion for inactivity never comes as a
    surprise: we email you <strong>30 days ahead</strong>. Coming back and doing a
    single activity keeps the account and resets the clock. And for as long as the
    account exists, you can download all of your data from
    <a href="<%= data_export_path %>" class="font-semibold underline" style="color: var(--brand);">My data</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    You don't have to wait for any of these deadlines, of course: you can ask us to
    delete your account at any time, and it happens immediately.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">8. Your rights</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">At any time, you can:</p>
  <ul class="mb-4 space-y-2 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
    <li>find out what data we hold about you and get a copy of it;</li>
    <li>have anything inaccurate corrected;</li>
    <li>ask us to delete your account and your data;</li>
    <li>object to a specific use, or ask for it to be restricted;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent to notifications, without this affecting the rest of the service.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    To exercise any of these, write to
    <a href="mailto:contato@practicebr.com" class="font-semibold underline" style="color: var(--brand);">contato@practicebr.com</a>.
    We reply within one month. If you believe your data is not handled properly, you
    have the right to lodge a complaint with the CNIL, the French data protection
    authority (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="underline" style="color: var(--brand);">cnil.fr</a>),
    or with the supervisory authority of the country where you live.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">9. Minors</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    If the student is under 15, the account must be created and authorised by a
    parent, legal guardian or school. If we find that a minor's account was opened
    without that authorisation, we delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">10. Security</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    All traffic is encrypted (HTTPS), passwords are stored as hashes and access to
    the database is restricted. No system is perfect: if an incident puts your data
    at risk, we will inform you and notify the competent authority within the legal
    deadline.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-deep);">11. Changes</h2>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    If this policy changes in any significant way, we will let you know by email
    before the change takes effect. The date at the top of the page always shows the
    version in force.
  </p>

</div>

<div class="text-center mt-10 pt-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--line);">
  <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--ink-soft);">
    Any questions about this? Write to us — we really do answer. 💚
  </p>
  <a href="mailto:contato@practicebr.com?subject=Privacy%20question%20-%20Practice-BR"
     class="btn btn-sm"
     style="background: var(--brand); color: var(--surface); border-color: var(--brand); font-weight: 600;">
    Get in touch
  </a>
  <div class="mt-6">
    <%= link_to "Back to home", root_path, class: "btn btn-ghost btn-sm", style: "color: var(--ink-faint);" %>
  </div>
</div>
